  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement] the outer halo = the law's phantom + the dust envelope, or the decomposition fails where, stated exactly
         measured: THE OUTER HALO AT CLUSTER SCALE = THE LAW'S PHANTOM + THE DUST ENVELOPE: V1 PASS, V2 FAIL.  Per cluster the law's A/r^2 (A from M_b(R500), zero parameters) was subtracted from the committed X-COP hydrostatic shells over the deep window (r_M, R500), r_M = 273-580 kpc on this convention.  V1: the pooled envelope slope is -2.38 +- 0.15 against the NFW-class prediction (-2.5, -2.0) -- INSIDE the band; per-cluster slopes span -7.15 .. +2.31 (in-band 2/12 clusters).  V2: the phantom exceeds the residual in 34/292 window bins (-- the subtraction is unphysical there).  The crossover r_x where rho_ph = rho_dust: numeric in-window crossings at A3266:1004; the task-formula prediction (A/rho_dust_scale)^(1/2) at ref r_M gives 484 kpc median (256-2720).  THE HONEST END: the decomposition does not fully close: the phantom asks for mass the residual does not carry -- the decomposition fails at the amplitude side (the r_M equipartition: M_ph(<r_M) = M_b(R500) exceeds the observed dark mass there in 34/292 of the window bins).  The amplitude of the dust envelope and the EFE cap line stay the registered open numbers (KEPLER_GRADE 'open numbers'); the raw residual slope on this deep window alone is median -2.29, vs the certified -1.53 on the 75-420 kpc straddling window (g04a/G008).
         reading : the FAILs above are the finding; the lane's registered numbers: pooled envelope slope, the negative-bin count, the crossover radii

